      "title": "Period VI: Religious Rulership & Fall",
      "subtitle": "Holy Crusade of Nemeth, Child Crucifixion, & Coup",
      "tags": [
        "History",
        "Chronology",
        "Lore",
        "period-vi"
      ],
      "aliases": [
        "Period VI: Religious Rulership & Fall",
        "period vi"
      ],
      "summary": "In the wake of the Starfall, Fergus launched a holy crusade across the Zingg Valley in the name of Nemeth the Gnostic, using divine magic to drive the zombie hordes back from the ruined capital. The theological foundation of this crusade was forged around the martyred cult leader who had died in the ritual fires. A strict theocratic regime was established over the realm. The church's authority was solidified when the prominent religious leader Falmouth discovered the legendary Fountain of Youth, granting miraculous longevity to the high priesthood.",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Chronological Designation:</strong> Period VI: Religious Rulership & Fall</p>\n  <p><strong>Core Theme:</strong> Holy Crusade of Nemeth, Child Crucifixion, & Coup</p>\n</div>\n<h3>Historical Chronicle</h3>\n<p>In the wake of the Starfall, Fergus launched a holy crusade across the Zingg Valley in the name of Nemeth the Gnostic, using divine magic to drive the zombie hordes back from the ruined capital. The theological foundation of this crusade was forged around the martyred cult leader who had died in the ritual fires. A strict theocratic regime was established over the realm. The church's authority was solidified when the prominent religious leader Falmouth discovered the legendary Fountain of Youth, granting miraculous longevity to the high priesthood.</p>\n<p>However, the church's absolute moral authority dissolved into widespread horror following the public crucifixion of a child. A fragile coalition of monarchists and republicans overthrew the church, driving them underground. As victory was achieved, a covert betrayal occurred: the head of the royal army conspired with the chief monarchist leader to assassinate the primary republican leader, framing the remnant church for the murder to crush republican momentum and consolidate monarchist political control.</p>\n\n",
      "gmSecrets": "Events from Period VI: Religious Rulership & Fall directly inform modern conspiracies, buried relics, and subterranean passages in The Pit.",
