      "summary": "General Don Rodrigo requests the Triumvirate sign an official royal decree mobilizing troops to purge a 'rebel encampment' in the Zingg Vall...",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Involved Factions:</strong> Military Elite, Republican Insurgents, The Triumvirate</p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic Reward:</strong> Saves key witnesses to Period VI state crimes, earning the secret allegiance of urban republican cells without triggering an immediate military coup.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Narrative Premise</h3>\n<p>General Don Rodrigo requests the Triumvirate sign an official royal decree mobilizing troops to purge a 'rebel encampment' in the Zingg Valley. In reality, the camp houses surviving witnesses to the Period VI assassination of the republican founder.</p>\n\n<h3>Core Conflict &amp; Player Choice</h3>\n<p>The PCs must decide whether to rubber-stamp the order to maintain Don Rodrigo's favor, or delay the decree to dispatch covert agents to investigate who is actually in the camp.</p>\n\n<div class=\"dc-box\">\n  <strong>Basic D&D Challenge Checks:</strong> Intelligence check (or 1-2 on 1d6) to uncover target camp; Charisma check to countermand military orders..\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"escalation\"><strong>Dynamic Escalation Trigger:</strong> If the PCs delay signing for more than 24 hours, Don Rodrigo executes the operation using his private household guard and places the royal quarters on protective lockdown.</p>\n",
